text Errors that involve a conflict in expressed semantics @17,35393,694,20
text Similarly, to draw the author's attention to mistakes in the use of elements, clear contradictions in the semantics expressed are also considered conformance errors. @17,35425,694,40
text In the fragments below, for example, the semantics are nonsensical: a separator cannot simultaneously be a cell, nor can a radio button be a progress bar. @17,35477,694,41
