text Cases where the default styles are likely to lead to confusion @17,36277,694,20
text Certain elements have default styles or behaviors that make certain combinations likely to lead to confusion. Where these have equivalent alternatives without this problem, the confusing combinations are disallowed. @17,36309,694,61
text For example, elements are rendered as , and elements as . Putting a in an is unnecessarily confusing; since either nesting just elements, or nesting just elements, or nesting elements inside elements all serve the same purpose as nesting a element in a element, but only the latter involves a in an , the latter combination is disallowed. @17,36382,694,81
